Attribution and branding condition:

Webin Cloud Server lets administrators change the application's branding (app
name, title, logo, icon, favicon and theme) from the Admin Panel. This is
permitted and encouraged.

However, the footer that credits the original author and the "Webin Cloud
Server" name (the Footer component of the frontend and the footer.* strings in
the locale files) must not be removed, hidden or altered in the source code,
in builds, or in redistributed copies, including modified versions and
container images. Changing the branding through the application's own
settings does not affect this footer, and that is the only supported way to
rebrand the application. The purpose of this condition is that the original
author and the name of the software remain visible to users of any
redistributed version.

